   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## QuantFunc Qwen-Image-2.1\n\n- **QuantFunc Qwen-Image-2.1 Loader** replaces the official `Load Diffusion Model` (UNETLoader): the QuantFunc engine runs the 32-block transformer; the text encoder (`CLIPLoader`, type `qwen_image`), `TextEncodeQwenImage21`, the VAE, the sampler and CFG stay stock ComfyUI.\n- `transformer`: the QuantFunc int4 export under `models/diffusion_models`; `model_config`: `qwen-image-2.1-int4`.\n- `quality`: on GPUs that offer `fast` and `super_fast`, `balance` (default) can be a little faster than `best_quality`, and `fast` and `super_fast` are usually faster still; with these three the picture stays the same, but details such as poses, faces or small objects can differ from `best_quality`. `best_quality` gives the highest quality. On other GPUs the loader shows no quality choice and always uses the highest quality.\n- Output is **RGBA**: `VAE Decode` + `Save Image` keep the alpha channel, so a transparent result saves as a transparent PNG.\n- Official settings: 25 steps, CFG 1, euler / simple (40 steps = the diffusers default, a little sharper).\n\n**Image edit (one reference).** `TextEncodeQwenImage21` sees the reference through the text encoder AND splices its VAE latent into the sequence (so it needs the VAE). Refer to it as `<image1>`. The output size follows the reference (the node's `latent` output)."
   ]
  },
